# Plugin Development Standards

## Objective
Establish secure, maintainable, and performant patterns for developing plugins in the Downlodr ecosystem while ensuring system stability and user safety.

## Context
- Extensible plugin architecture with secure sandboxing
- TypeScript-based plugin API with strong typing
- Dynamic loading and unloading of plugins
- Cross-platform compatibility requirements
- Security-first approach to third-party code execution

## Rules

### Plugin Architecture

#### Plugin Structure
- **Standard manifest**: Every plugin must have a manifest.json
- **Entry point consistency**: Use standard entry point naming
- **TypeScript support**: Prefer TypeScript for plugin development
  ```typescript
  ✅ // manifest.json
  {
    "id": "format-converter",
    "name": "Format Converter",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Convert downloads between different formats",
    "main": "index.ts",
    "author": "Plugin Author",
    "license": "MIT",
    "minAppVersion": "1.7.0",
    "icon": "icon.png"
  }
  
  ✅ // index.ts - Plugin entry point
  export const plugin: DownlodrPlugin = {
    id: 'format-converter',
    name: 'Format Converter',
    version: '1.0.0',
    description: 'Convert downloads between different formats',
    author: 'Plugin Author',
    
    async initialize(api: PluginAPI) {
      // Plugin initialization
    },
    
    async onUnload() {
      // Cleanup logic
    }
  };
  
  ❌ // Non-standard structure
  export default function() { /* plugin code */ }
  ```

#### Plugin Interface Implementation
- **Standard interface**: Implement the DownlodrPlugin interface
- **Proper initialization**: Handle initialization and cleanup properly
- **Error handling**: Include comprehensive error handling
  ```typescript
  ✅ export const plugin: DownlodrPlugin = {
    id: 'my-plugin',
    name: 'My Plugin',
    version: '1.0.0',
    description: 'Plugin description',
    author: 'Author Name',
    
    async initialize(api: PluginAPI): Promise<void> {
      try {
        // Register plugin features
        await this.registerFeatures(api);
        
        // Set up event listeners
        this.setupEventListeners(api);
        
        console.log(`${this.name} initialized successfully`);
      } catch (error) {
        console.error(`Failed to initialize ${this.name}:`, error);
        throw error;
      }
    },
    
    async onUnload(): Promise<void> {
      // Clean up resources
      this.removeEventListeners();
      this.disposeResources();
    }
  };
  
  ❌ // Incomplete implementation
  export const plugin = {
    initialize() {
      // Minimal initialization without error handling
    }
  };
  ```

### Plugin API Usage

#### API Access Patterns
- **Use provided APIs**: Only use APIs exposed through the PluginAPI
- **Respect boundaries**: Don't access application internals directly
- **Type safety**: Use TypeScript interfaces for API calls
  ```typescript
  ✅ // Proper API usage
  async function registerDownloadHandler(api: PluginAPI) {
    api.downloads.registerDownloadSource({
      id: 'custom-source',
      name: 'Custom Source',
      matcher: (url: string) => url.includes('custom-site.com'),
      handler: async (url: string) => {
        return await processCustomDownload(url);
      }
    });
  }
  
  ✅ // UI extension
  function addUIExtension(api: PluginAPI) {
    api.ui.addTaskbarButton({
      id: 'my-button',
      label: 'My Feature',
      icon: 'icon-name',
      onClick: () => handleButtonClick()
    });
  }
  
  ❌ // Direct access to internals
  const mainStore = window.electronAPI.getMainStore(); // Don't access directly
  ```

#### Event Handling
- **Subscribe to events**: Use the event system for reactive behavior
- **Clean event listeners**: Always clean up event listeners
- **Error handling**: Handle events gracefully
  ```typescript
  ✅ class PluginEventManager {
    private unsubscribeFunctions: Array<() => void> = [];
    
    setupEventListeners(api: PluginAPI): void {
      const unsubscribeProgress = api.downloads.onDownloadProgress((event) => {
        try {
          this.handleProgressUpdate(event);
        } catch (error) {
          console.error('Error handling progress update:', error);
        }
      });
      
      this.unsubscribeFunctions.push(unsubscribeProgress);
    }
    
    cleanup(): void {
      this.unsubscribeFunctions.forEach(unsubscribe => unsubscribe());
      this.unsubscribeFunctions = [];
    }
  }
  
  ❌ // No cleanup
  api.downloads.onDownloadProgress((event) => {
    // Handle event without storing unsubscribe function
  });
  ```

### UI Extensions

#### Component Registration
- **Standard component patterns**: Follow established UI patterns
- **Responsive design**: Ensure components work across screen sizes
- **Accessibility**: Include proper accessibility attributes
  ```typescript
  ✅ function registerModalExtension(api: PluginAPI) {
    api.ui.registerModal({
      id: 'plugin-settings',
      title: 'Plugin Settings',
      component: SettingsModal,
      size: 'md',
      closable: true,
      callbacks: {
        onMount: () => console.log('Modal mounted'),
        onUnmount: () => console.log('Modal unmounted')
      }
    });
  }
  
  ✅ const SettingsModal: React.FC<PluginModalProps> = ({ pluginId, onClose }) => {
    return (
      <div className="space-y-4">
        <h2 className="text-lg font-semibold">Settings</h2>
        <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
          {/* Form content */}
        </form>
      </div>
    );
  };
  
  ❌ // Non-standard component
  const BadModal = () => <div>Settings</div>;
  ```

#### Side Panel Extensions
- **Consistent layout**: Follow side panel layout guidelines
- **State management**: Properly manage component state
- **Integration**: Integrate well with existing UI
  ```typescript
